**Time complexity to remember:**

* Usually `O(n)` because each pointer moves through the array at most once.
* Two nested-looking pointer movements can still be `O(n)` if the pointers only move forward.
* `3Sum` is typically `O(n²)` because of sorting + a two-pointer scan for each element.

### ⭐ Key idea to remember

Don't memorize the template as:

```text
left++
right--
```

Remember:

> **Two pointers work when I can decide which pointer to move based on the current values/condition.**

That's the actual pattern you need to recognize in placement problems.
